\DOC REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC

\TYPE {REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Strips all leading universal quantifiers from the goal's conclusion, leaving
the body as a single new goal.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is {!x1 ... xn. t}, it
removes the entire prefix of universal quantifiers in one step, specialising
the bound variables to free variables of the same names. The body {t} —
including any implication, its antecedents and consequent — is otherwise
unchanged.
{
   A ?- !x1 ... xn. t
   =================== REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC
         A ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the only effect is this quantifier stripping, with no
further change to the conclusion, and the goals involved have no assumptions
and bodies that are implications leading to an {ensures} statement.

\ENDDOC
